/ActualText (Method hiding is a concept in object-oriented programming where a subclass defines a method with the same name as a method in its superclass, but the subclass method doesn't override the superclass method. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Instead, it creates a new, independent method with the same name. This can lead to confusion and unexpected behavior, so it's generally recommended to use method overriding instead.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
